  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$",
